cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Parity: certified vocabulary augmentation without continued pretraining"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Parity contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/NagaYu/parity"
url: "https://huggingface.co/spaces/NagaYu/parity"
abstract: >-
  Parity adds language-specific tokens to an already-trained open-weight
  language model, synthesises their embeddings from the model's own internal
  representations by subspace-restricted Gauss-Newton least squares, and ships a
  distribution-free certificate bounding how far the model's behaviour can move.
  No continued pretraining is performed; every model parameter stays frozen.
  Token ids are append-only, so requests served under the base tokenizer view are
  bit-for-bit identical to the original model, and a single model instance can
  serve many tokenizer views with a shared prefix cache.
keywords:
  - tokenizer
  - vocabulary adaptation
  - multilingual
  - inference efficiency
  - conformal prediction
  - submodular optimization
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-16"
